From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:24:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] feat(harbor_agent): OpenCode adapter for in-pod GRPO
 runs (pinned 1.17.11)

OpenCodeNemoGym gets the run command, environment, configuration and
install it needs to run inside a task sandbox under token capture. All
OpenCode keys and flags were checked against the OpenCode source at tag
v1.17.11 (anomalyco/opencode 67aec2212); comments cite file:line there.

Run command:
  set -o pipefail; [timeout -k 10 <T>] opencode --model nemogym/<m> run
  --format=json --title 'NeMo Gym' [--print-logs --log-level DEBUG]
  -- <instruction> 2>&1 </dev/null | tee /logs/agent/opencode.txt
- </dev/null: with a non-TTY stdin `opencode run` reads stdin to EOF
  before anything else (cli/cmd/run.ts:399); the sandbox exec leaves it
  open. Likely cause of the 900 s silence in job 5236016.
- --title: a non-default title skips the title model call.
- pipefail keeps OpenCode's exit status (124 from timeout) for
  return-code.txt; the timeout wrapper is opt-in (opencode_timeout_sec).

Config (OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT), so that only the main loop calls the
model (a second root masks a capture rollout without a witness):
enabled_providers [nemogym]; provider options timeout/headerTimeout
false (stream replay sends no byte before generation ends; a timed-out
request would be retried as another captured call); model limit from
model_info (output capped by max_output_tokens of the request);
agent.title.disable; agent.build.steps = max_turns; compaction auto and
prune off; snapshot off; permission "*" allow, task/webfetch/websearch/
todowrite deny (denied tools leave the request's tool list). The
opencode_config kwarg is deep-merged last (None deletes a key).

Env: XDG_DATA_HOME=/logs/agent/opencode-data (DB and logs come back
with the trial), OPENCODE_DISABLE_MODELS_FETCH/_AUTOUPDATE/
_PROJECT_CONFIG, OPENCODE_EXPERIMENTAL_OUTPUT_TOKEN_MAX, OPENCODE_FAKE_VCS.
OPENCODE_DISABLE_SHARE does not exist in 1.17.11 (config share:
disabled instead).

Install: default (opencode_install: binary) downloads the standalone
glibc binary opencode-linux-x64-baseline.tar.gz of the pinned release
with python3 (curl fallback), checks sha256 (known digest for 1.17.11,
or opencode_sha256), installs to /usr/local/bin and checks --version;
skips when that version is already there. opencode_install: npm keeps
Harbor's nvm/npm script. version defaults to 1.17.11.

responses_create_params, max_turns and model_info are now explicit
kwargs. Sampling values are still not sent by OpenCode; set them with
vllm_model.sampling_overrides.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
